*******************************************************************************************                                                                                        **		Apple IIgs Printer Driver                                                        **                                                                                        **		File: imager.a -- Low Level Driver: Host pixmap > Printer data                   **                                                                                        **		Written by Ben Koning                                                            **		Copyright (C) 1991 Apple Computer, Inc.                                          **                                                                                        *******************************************************************************************							include		'equates.h'																												include		'm16.util'							include		'm16.intmath'							include		'm16.event'							include		'm16.misctool'							include		'e16.quickdraw'ImagerProc					proc		export**IMAGER: LOW-LEVEL PRINTER DRIVER ROUTINES**These routines are the only ones which communicate with the printer device.  They are*capable of providing paper motion control and a process of marking the paper with the*image of a bitmap supplied by the caller, in various resolutions (that is, various*sizes).  It is the intention that the caller request that the imager mark the page in*a high resolution with a large bitmap, the latter compensating for the former so that*the resulting image appears at the correct size, but with increased resolution.**This particular imager is feature-reduced and does not support color.  Instead, it is*optimized for speed performance by means of white space skipping, direct source pixel*to printer pixel conversion, and data compression.**The following entry points are offered:**	ImagerOpen				Establishes unique connection to printer; must be called first*	ImagerSetLocInfo		Sets up locinfo struct of bitmap to print; should be called second*	ImagerSetGrays			Sets up pixel conversion table using screen color table settings*	ImagerSetFeed			Sets up for automatic or manual paper feed*	ImagerSetResolution		Sets up dpi-quality (size of each printer pixel)*	ImagerSetVCondense		Sets up double or single vertical stretching*	ImagerSetIdleProc		Sets up idle proc to be called periodically*	ImagerSetAbortPoll		Sets up address to listen for to cause abort*	ImagerGetVAlignFactor	Returns vertical size to which bitmap must be aligned*	ImagerReady				Must be called after Set and before Formfeed/Linefeed/Print calls*	ImagerFormfeed			Outputs a form feed character*	ImagerLinefeed			Moves the paper down by a specified distance*	ImagerPrint				Images, compresses, and sends a graphics bitmap*	ImagerClose				Releases unique connection to printer; must be called last**The imager, like other modules of the print driver, uses "ParamXXXXY" direct*page variables defined in the equates module.**Entry points that require pointers should be called with the low word in X*and the high word in Y.  Entry points that require input values should be*called with the A register set.  Output, if any, is given in the A register*and carry flag.**Imager calls MUST be made in the following sequence:**	(1) ImagerOpen, required to allocate resources and set up defaults*	(2) ImagerSetLocInfo, required first because other calls need its information*	(3) ImagerSetGrays, required before printing but after ImagerSetLocInfo*	(4) Any mixture of the other Get/Set calls, to change to nondefault settings*	(5) ImagerReady, required before printing because it transmits settings to device*	(6) Any mixture of ImagerFormfeed/ImagerLinefeed/ImagerPrint calls, which mark the paper*	(7) ImagerClose, required to deallocate resources**Normally, the ImagerPrint routine returns with 0 in the accumulator.  If the*accumulator is nonzero then there was a user-abort request or irrecoverable*problem, and the print job must be aborted.  If the accumulator is nonzero on*exit then the carry flag is also set.**Error codes returned in A/carry by ImagerPrint are as follows:**	$0080	User abort, because of Cmd-'.' press or AbortPoll being asserted*	$008F	Communications or printer protocol error**While processing raster lines, an internal routine is called periodically*which services various functions asynchronously.  It is then that the user-*installable IdleProc and AbortPoll are checked and called, as well as*command-period, communications, and printer error checks.**The address (if not NIL) given in ImagerSetIdleProc is called (JSL) with*our environment saved.  The Command-Period printing interrupt request from the*user is checked for even if a non-NIL address is given (Command-Period causes*the imager to abort and return $80 status).**The address (if not NIL) given in ImagerSetAbortPoll is checked after the*idleproc is executed; this allows a high-level driver to allow the idleproc*to set a global variable such as PrSetError.**The coordinates given in ImagerSetLocInfo must be such that Y1<Y2 and*X1<X2.  The X coordinates should be byte-aligned.  Mixed 640-and-320*modes within the same bitmap is not supported.  This call initializes*values used during printing, such as the color pixel conversion table*which maps screen pixels into printer pixels.**Within the chunky color pixels of the bitmap, the color table entries for*%00 or %0000 are assumed to be pure black and those for %11 or %1111 are*assumed to be pure white.  A pure black and a pure white should always*exist in the standard color table entries.  If this is not the case, then*those pixels in the bitmap which refer to %00/%0000 or %11/%1111 will be*incorrectly printed black or white, respectively.  Also, if there are*pure black/white colors, but assigned to nonstandard locations in the*color table, then printing may also be incorrect.**Notes on terminology: In these routines, "band" refers to one scan of the*print head.  Do not confuse this with the printing bands into which the*high-level driver print loop routines split up each page due to possible*memory constraints.  Also, note the distinctions made in the comments*between "source" and "printer" pixels.  "Source" pixels are the input to*the imager (and are in fact usually in an off-screen buffer), and "printer"*pixels are the dots which are sent to the printer device.***IMAGEROPEN: Establishes unique connection with printer and initializes the imager: Error -> carry:*							export ImagerOpenImagerOpen							stz AbortFlag						;zero our abort flag							stz Resolution						;default 180 dpi							stz PaperFeed						;default automatic paper feed							stz VerticalCondenseFlag			;default no vertical condense							stz IdleProcPtr+0					;default no idle procedure							stz IdleProcPtr+2							stz AbortPollPtr+0					;default no abort poll location							stz AbortPollPtr+2							stz PrinterVerticalPosition			;top of form														import CommOpen						;ask to open connection: this call							brl CommOpen						;sets or clears carry flag**IMAGERCLOSE: Releases unique connection with printer and terminates the imager:*							export ImagerCloseImagerClose							import CommClose					;ask to close connection							brl CommClose**IMAGERGETVALIGNFACTOR: Returns vert align needed for some printers with band print models -> A:*							export ImagerGetVAlignFactorImagerGetVAlignFactor							lda #ImagerQDPattVAlignFactor		;any-vertical-size bitmap is ok,							rts									;but allow for quickdraw patterns**IMAGERSETFEED: Informs us of automatic or manual paper feed.  Pass 0/1 for automatic/manual -> A:*							export ImagerSetFeedImagerSetFeed							and #%1								;do range clip for 0..1							sta PaperFeed						;set our global variable							rts**IMAGERSETLOCINFO: Informs us of bitmap dims with locinfo/inits color map table.  Ptr lo->X, hi->Y:*							export ImagerSetLocInfoImagerSetLocInfo							stx ParamLongA+0					;access caller's locinfo struct							sty ParamLongA+2							ldy #oportSCB						;obtain the current graphics mode							lda [ParamLongA],y					;and store as $00/$80 in static var							and #$0080							sta SourceMode														ldy #optrToPixImage					;obtain pointer to caller's bitmap							lda [ParamLongA],y					;and store in our static variable							sta SourcePixPtr+0							iny							iny							lda [ParamLongA],y							sta SourcePixPtr+2														ldy #owidth							;obtain byte-width and store							lda [ParamLongA],y							sta SourceByteWidth														ldy #oboundsRect+ov1				;store beginning and ending raster							lda [ParamLongA],y					;lines of the source bitmap; note							sta SourceYLineBegin				;that Y1 must be smaller than Y2							ldy #oboundsRect+ov2							lda [ParamLongA],y							sta SourceYLineEnd														ldy #oboundsRect+oh1				;convert beginning X coordinate to							lda [ParamLongA],y					;byte offset and store							and #%1111111111111000				;round down to multiple of 8							lsr a							ldx SourceMode						;320: 2 pix/byte, 640: 4 pix/byte							beq SeLoDivX1Its320SeLoDivX1Its640				lsr aSeLoDivX1Its320				sta SourceXByteBegin							ldy #oboundsRect+oh2				;convert ending X coordinate to							lda [ParamLongA],y					;byte offset and store							and #%1111111111111000				;round down to multiple of 8							lsr a							ldx SourceMode						;320: 2 pix/byte, 640: 4 pix/byte							beq SeLoDivX2Its320SeLoDivX2Its640				lsr aSeLoDivX2Its320				sta SourceXByteEnd							rts									;exit**IMAGERSETGRAYS: Inits pixel conversion lookup table, must be called after ImagerSetLocInfo:**This routine sets up the screen color to printer grayscale mapping.  This routine must be*called after ImagerSetLocInfo, so that it knows which mode (320/640) is in effect.  In 640*mode, black and white are mapped properly in addition to three arbitrarily mapped grays.*In 320 mode, the values of the current color table to establish halftone patterns.**The table that we build here, and which is used by the low-level pixel conversion loop, has*two parts which are identical in usage but may contain different values in order to implement*gray patterns.  Each part is capable of converting a byte of screen pixels into a nibble of*printer pixels.  Each part of the table thus has a domain of 8 bits and a range of 4 bits*(stored in 8-bit bytes).  The table parts are designed to be accessed with 8 bits of source*(screen) pixel data (2 or 4 pixels if 320/640), and return a nibble full of printer-ready pixels.*In 640 mode, 4 source pixels are mapped into 4 printer pixels.  In 320 mode, 2 source pixels are*doubled and are also mapped into 4 printer pixels.  Since we initialize the table for either mode*at this time, the imaging loop itself need only use this table and need not decide on the fly*which mode is in effect.**Two subroutines, MAP640PIXEL and MAP320PIXEL, are employed to perform the actual mapping of a*source pixel.  These routines are passed the source pixel bits in A, must return printer pixel*bits in A, must preserve Y, and may use X as a dither counter.  The output from these routines*is allowed to vary every other time to implement gray.**The MAP640PIXEL routine only needs to return a single 1-bit output (which may of course vary*over an every-other period for non-pure-black/white input values).  The MAP320PIXEL routine,*however, must output two separate 2-bit outputs, a primary and an alternate.  Since both*primary and alternate values are allowed to change every other time as well, the number of gray*possibilities is greatly increased.  Both parts of the lookup table are filled with the same*single output value from MAP640PIXEL if 640 mode is in effect; the primary and alternate parts*of the table are filled with the primary and alternate output values from MAP320PIXEL if 320*mode is in effect.*							export ImagerSetGraysImagerSetGrays							ldy #0								;Y has count, X used by map routinesbt_loop						lda SourceMode						;branch on 320/640 mode							beq bt_its320							bt_its640					tya									;get a possible byte full of src pix							and #%11							;rightmost src pix in b0,b1 -> pr b0							jsr Map640Pixel						;init, pwA will build pr pixels byte							sta ParamWordA														tya									;convert 3rd source pix -> pr pix							lsr a								;source pix b2,b3 -> print pix b1							lsr a							and #%11							jsr Map640Pixel							asl a							ora ParamWordA							sta ParamWordA														tya									;convert 2nd source pix -> pr pix							lsr a								;source pix b4,b5 -> print pix b2							lsr a							lsr a							lsr a							and #%11							jsr Map640Pixel							asl a							asl a							ora ParamWordA							sta ParamWordA														tya									;convert leftmost src pix -> pr pix							lsr a								;source pix b6,b7 -> print pix b3							lsr a							lsr a							lsr a							lsr a							lsr a							and #%11							jsr Map640Pixel							asl a							asl a							asl a							ora ParamWordA														sta ParamWordA						;store same final result in pwA/pwB							sta ParamWordB						;so that both parts of the table							bra bt_next							;will have the parallel values							bt_its320					tya									;convert rightmost pix in byte							and #%1111							;source b0-b3 -> print b0 and b1							jsr Map320Pixel						;for both primary/alternate tables							pha							and #%11							sta ParamWordA							pla							xba							and #%11							sta ParamWordB														tya									;convert leftmost pix in byte							lsr a								;source b4-b7 -> print b2 and b3							lsr a								;for both primary/alternate tables							lsr a							lsr a							and #%1111							jsr Map320Pixel							pha							and #%11							asl a							asl a							ora ParamWordA							sta ParamWordA							pla							xba							and #%11							asl a							asl a							ora ParamWordB							sta ParamWordB							bt_next						shortm								;get pwA/pwB primary/alternate							lda	ParamWordA						;nibbles full of print pixels							sta SourceToPrintPixLookup+000,y	;store into a pri/alt tables bytes							lda ParamWordB							sta SourceToPrintPixLookup+256,y							longm							iny									;goto next possibility of src byte							cpy #256							;go create all possible values of							beq bt_exit							;source byte; when done, exit							brl bt_loopbt_exit						rts**Subroutine to convert one 640-mode pixel into one print pixel: In/Out -> A, preserves Y, uses X:**This routine must preserve the Y register and may assume that the X register does not change*between invocations of this routine, so that it can use it as a dither counter.  Two bits go*into this routine, and one bit comes out.**Input format given in A:		640-mode pixel in bits b0-b1; other bits zeros*Output format required in A:	One bit of printer pixel data in b0; other bits zeros*Map640Pixel					and #%11							;look at a 640 chunky pix in lo bits							beq m6_its_black					;branch if source is pure black							cmp #%11							;compare for pure white							beq m6_its_white					;branch if source is pure white							inx									;else it's in between, so alternate							txa									;increment wild count, consider as							and #%1								;alternating black/white if even/odd							beq m6_its_blackm6_its_white				lda #%0								;white source pix -> no ink pr pix							rtsm6_its_black				lda #%1								;black source pix -> yes ink pr pix							rts**Subroutine to convert one 320-mode pixel into two print pixels: In/Out -> A, preserves Y, uses X:**This routine must preserve the Y register and may assume that the X register does not change*between invocations of this routine, so that it can use it as a dither counter.  Four bits go*into this routine, and two alternatives of two bits each comes out.**Input format given in A:		320-mode pixel in bits b0-b3; other bits zeros*Output format required in A:	Two sets of two bits of pr pix in b0-b1 and b8-b9; other bits zeros*Map320Pixel					phx									;save free running counter														and #%1111							;mask off garbage, have one 320 pix							asl a								;each color entry is 2 bytes							sta m3_temp							;save offset within palette for a sec														lda >$E19D00+100					;look at SCB for line 100							and #%1111							;isolate color palette 0..15							asl a								;times 32, each palette is 32 bytes							asl a							asl a							asl a							asl a								;now have index to palette							clc							adc m3_temp							;add which pix color within palette							tax							lda >$E19E00,x						;get $0RGB color for this pixel														pha									;do K=(5R+8G+3B)/16							xba							and #$F								;R							sta m3_temp							asl a							asl a								;4*R							clc							adc m3_temp							;5*R							sta m3_temp							lda 1,s							lsr a							and #%0000000001111000				;8*G							clc							adc m3_temp							;5*R + 8*G							sta m3_temp							lda 1,s							and #$F								;B							sta 1,s							asl a								;2*B							clc							adc 1,s								;3*B							sta 1,s							pla							clc							adc m3_temp							;5*R + 8*G + 3*B							lsr a							lsr a							lsr a							lsr a								;(5*R + 8*G + 3*B) / 16																					plx									;restore free running counter							phx									;but keep it saved														and #%1111							;we now have 0..15 density							asl a								;multiply by 4 because							asl a								;all table entries are 4 bytes wide							sta m3_temp							;save table index for a moment							txa									;get free running counter							and #%1								;isolate its even-odd status							asl a								;times 2: now have 0,2,0,2...							clc									;add this to table index, now have							adc m3_temp							;table entry + 0,2,0,2... index							tax									;now get two bytes from table entry,							lda m3_table,x						;w/ 2 bits in b0-b1 & 2 bits in b8-b9														plx									;restore/increment counter and exit							inx									;note that next time we'll get the							rts									;other two bytes from table entry							m3_table					dc.b %11,%11,%11,%11				;0 screen	15 print	black							dc.b %11,%11,%11,%01				;1			14							dc.b %11,%11,%01,%01				;2			13							dc.b %11,%11,%01,%01				;3			12							dc.b %11,%01,%11,%01				;4			11							dc.b %01,%01,%01,%01				;5			10							dc.b %11,%01,%00,%01				;6			9							dc.b %11,%11,%00,%00				;7			8			gray							dc.b %01,%01,%01,%00				;8			7			gray							dc.b %01,%11,%00,%00				;9			6							dc.b %11,%00,%11,%00				;10			5							dc.b %01,%01,%00,%00				;11			4							dc.b %01,%01,%00,%00				;12			3							dc.b %01,%00,%00,%00				;13			2							dc.b %01,%00,%00,%00				;14			1							dc.b %00,%00,%00,%00				;15 screen	0 print		white							m3_temp						dc.w 0**IMAGERSETRESOLUTION: Sets size of each printer pixel to 180/360 dpi.  Pass 0/1 -> ACC:*							export ImagerSetResolutionImagerSetResolution							and #1								;do rudamentary range clip							sta Resolution						;store it in global static var							rts**IMAGERSETVCONDENSE: Sets up 2x/1x-vert-size to compensate for GS fonts.  Pass 0/1: no/yes -> ACC:*							export ImagerSetVCondenseImagerSetVCondense							and #%1								;make sure it's only 0 or 1							sta VerticalCondenseFlag			;store it in global static var							rts**IMAGERSETIDLEPROC: Sets proc to be called during printing.  Pass ptr or NIL lo->X, hi->Y:*							export ImagerSetIdleProcImagerSetIdleProc							stx IdleProcPtr+0							sty IdleProcPtr+2							rts**IMAGERSETABORTPOLL: Sets adrs; if goes non-0 during print, we abort.  Pass ptr/NIL lo->X, hi->Y:*							export ImagerSetAbortPollImagerSetAbortPoll							stx AbortPollPtr+0							sty AbortPollPtr+2							rts**IMAGERREADY: Sets up printer's controller: Pass 0/1 for normal/inhibit-reset-command -> ACC:*							export ImagerReadyImagerReady							cmp #0								;check if ACC nonzero							bne ImRe_reset_done					;if nonzero don't do general reset							lda #ImReResetCommand				;general printer reset command							import CommWriteShort				;causes head calibration motion							jsr CommWriteShort					;and sets defaults in printerImRe_reset_done														ldx PaperFeed						;send command to select paper							beq ImRe_feed_auto					;feed mode; the printer's paperImRe_feed_man				lda #ImReManFeedCommand				;loading behavior is slightly							bra ImRe_feed_set					;different for the manual modeImRe_feed_auto				lda #ImReAutoFeedCommand							import CommWriteShortImRe_feed_set				jsr CommWriteShort														stz PrinterVerticalPosition			;set top/form for our Y accounting														ldx Resolution						;send command to select one of the							beq ImRe_res_180					;resolution modes; the higher theImRe_res_360				lda	#ImRe360DPIUniCommand			;resolution, the smaller the pr pix							bra ImRe_res_set					;and select head motion optionImRe_res_180				lda #ImRe180DPIBiCommand							import CommWriteShortImRe_res_set				jsr CommWriteShort							rts							ImReResetCommand			dc.b 4							dc.b $FF,$FF,$FF,$49				;immediate general resetImReAutoFeedCommand			dc.b 1								;automatic paper feed							dc.b $41ImReManFeedCommand			dc.b 1								;manual paper feed							dc.b $4DImRe360DPIUniCommand		dc.b 2							dc.b $6E							;360 dpi "normal" resolution							dc.b $75							;unidirectional head motionImRe180DPIBiCommand			dc.b 2							dc.b $64							;180 dpi "draft" resolution							dc.b $3C							;bidirectional head motion**IMAGERFORMFEED: Causes the printer to eject the current page:*							export ImagerFormfeedImagerFormfeed							stz PrinterVerticalPosition			;our accouting of vert position							lda #ImFfFormfeedCommand			;send form feed command							import CommWriteShort							brl CommWriteShortImFfFormfeedCommand			dc.b 1							dc.b $0C**IMAGERLINEFEED: Moves position on paper down by a specified distance.  Pass distance -> ACC:*							export ImagerLinefeedImagerLinefeed							clc									;add given value to our accounting							adc PrinterVerticalPosition			;of current vertical position, to							sta	PrinterVerticalPosition			;be used for next define-rect cmd							rts **IMAGERPRINT: Converts/compresses/sends bitmap referred by locinfo.  ACC/c -> Abort status:**This routine converts the bitmap that has been previously specified with the set-locinfo call*into printer-ready pixels and causes it to be printed.  In doing so, we employ a fast white*scanner and utilize the pixel conversion table that was set up with the BuildPixConvertTable*routine.  CompressSend is called each time after the printer-pix-buffer has been filled by the*completed processing of the current raster line.  After many CompressSend calls, we also*periodically call IntraLineService and terminate the imaging process if necessary.**This routine provides two error paths: This routine may return a nonzero status in A/carry,*indicating an unrecoverable error, in which case the entire print job should always be aborted.*In addition, if a recoverable error is detected, the optional caller's error procedure is*called with an error code in A.**Variables used within the scope of doing all lines:*	ParamLongD has pointer to beginning of current source line; it is inc by source width*	ParamWordE has count of number of source lines that have been processed so far**Variables within the scope of each line:*	Y register has index into next byte position of source-pixel-buffer from ParamLongD*	ParamWordF has index into next available byte of printer-pixel-buffer*	ParamWordD is nonzero at the end of the current source line if it's not fully blank*							export ImagerPrintImagerPrint*Do intraline service to allow abort and check for errors before doing DDR:							jsr IntraLineService							lda AbortFlag							beq ImPr_done_beforeDDRcheck							brl ImPr_exitImPr_done_beforeDDRcheck							*Send define-graphics-rectangle command so printer firmware knows where paper is to be marked:  							lda SourceXByteBegin				;set X1 limits in coordinates							asl a								;convert from screen-byte offsets							asl a								;to printer coordinates: one screen							sta ImPrRectCommandX1				;byte will ALWAYS map to 4 pr pix														lda SourceXByteEnd					;set X2 limits in coordinates							asl a							asl a							dea									;for n pixels, set limits in the							sta ImPrRectCommandX2				;form of 0..n-1														lda PrinterVerticalPosition			;Y limits are in raster lines  							sta ImPrRectCommandY1				;y1 = beyond end of last rect														lda SourceYLineEnd					;y2 = y1 + (tallness of this current							sec									;ImagerPrint call * 2 if vertical							sbc SourceYLineBegin				;condense is off since we map each							ldx VerticalCondenseFlag			;source line into two printer lines							bne ImPr_rectY2_GotTallness			;if vertical condense is off) - 1							asl a								;so that the first rect will beImPr_rectY2_GotTallness		dea									;0..199, for example, and the next							clc									;will be 200..399, etc.							adc ImPrRectCommandY1							sta ImPrRectCommandY2							ina									;also save position one line below							sta PrinterVerticalPosition			;bottom of rect for next time														lda #ImPrRectCommand				;do define-graphics-rect (DDR) cmd							import CommWriteShort							jsr CommWriteShort							*Do intraline service to allow abort and check for errors after DDR (paper might be empty, etc):							jsr IntraLineService							lda AbortFlag							beq ImPr_done_afterDDRcheck							brl ImPr_exitImPr_done_afterDDRcheck							*Initialize vertical loop counters:							pha									;setup plD with address of starting							pha									;source raster line by doing							pushword SourceYLineBegin			;(y1 * raster_width) + pix_map_base							pushword SourceByteWidth							_Multiply							clc									;prepare to add							pla									;get lo word of multiply result							adc SourcePixPtr+0					;add to pix map base and store lo							sta ParamLongD+0							pla									;get hi word of multiply result							adc SourcePixPtr+2					;add to pix map base and store hi							sta ParamLongD+2														lda SourceYLineBegin				;reset vertical line counter in pwE							sta ParamWordE*Head of vertical loop for doing all raster lines:ImPr_vertical_loop*Init for converting one horizontal source-pixel line into a printer-pixel line:							stz ParamWordD						;reset line-dirty flag in pwD							stz ParamWordF						;reset print-pix-buffer index in pwF							jsr ClearPrintPixBuffer				;zero the print-pix-buffer itself							lda SourceXByteEnd					;reset end-of-source-line terminator							sta ImPr_white_eoln+1				;in the white-elimination loop							ldy SourceXByteBegin				;reset source-pix-line index in Y							*Do fast loop which scans across white space a word at a time:ImPr_white_loop				lda [ParamLongD],y					;get a word-full of source pixels							cmp #$FFFF							;compare for all-std-white pixels							bne ImPr_not_white					;go mark the pr buffer if not whiteImPr_white_next				inc ParamWordF						;increment index into pr pix buffer							iny									;increment for getting next src word							inyImPr_white_eoln				cpy #$0000							;NOTE: operand is stuffed							bcc ImPr_white_loop					;loop until out of bytes in src line							bra ImPr_done_converting			;branch if done with all bytes*A source pixel word containing at least one non-white pixel has been encountered:ImPr_not_white*Cvt word-full of src pix in A to byte-full of pr pix, store in pr-pix-buff, set line-dirty flag:							phy									;save 16-bit Y which has src h index							sep #$20+$10						;set shortm+shortx: 8 bit mem/A/X/Y							tax									;left src byte in A, right in B							lda SourceToPrintPixLookup+000,x	;lo src byte -> 4 bits of pr pixels							asl a								;shift into position; lo src byte's							asl a								;pr pix nibble will be the high							asl a								;nibble of the pr pix byte that we're							asl a								;currently forming							sta ParamWordA						;this will become lo nibble of pr pix							xba									;now get high (right) source byte							tax									;get 8 bits of source pixels in X							lda SourceToPrintPixLookup+256,x	;hi src byte -> 4 bits of pr pixels							ora ParamWordA						;bring in low nibble already obtained							rep #$10							;longx; back to 16-bit for buff index							ldx ParamWordF						;get current index into line buffer							sta PrintPixBuffer,x				;store 8 bits of print pixels							ora ParamWordD						;since A is now nonzero, ensure that							sta ParamWordD						;the line-dirty flag gets/stays set							rep #$20							;longm; now everything back to 16-bit							ply									;restore 16-bit Y with src h index							bra	ImPr_white_next					;inc/loop back to white or this again*Done with converting a single raster.  We now have a full line of printer-ready pixels:ImPr_done_converting*If fully empty, send do-blank-line command without having to do compression encoding:							lda ParamWordD						;skip if nonzero; else if zero, then							bne ImPr_not_blankline				;there are no pr pix on this line							lda VerticalCondenseFlag			;if vertical condense is on, then							bne ImPr_blank_vert_1X				;every single src line prints as oneImPr_blank_vert_2X			lda #ImPrBlankLineCommand			;line, else, prints as two pr lines							import CommWriteShort							jsr CommWriteShortImPr_blank_vert_1X			lda #ImPrBlankLineCommand							import CommWriteShort							jsr CommWriteShort							bra ImPr_done_sendingImPr_not_blankline*Else compress and send a dirty line of print-pixel data to printer:							jsr CompressSend					;compact and send pr-line-buff data							lda VerticalCondenseFlag			;if vertical condense is on, then							bne ImPr_dirty_vert_1X				;every single src line prints as oneImPr_dirty_vert_2X			lda #ImPrRepeatLineCommand			;line, else, prints as two pr lines							import CommWriteShort							jsr CommWriteShortImPr_dirty_vert_1X*We have now finished sending a single raster to the printer:ImPr_done_sending*Periodically do print-time activities: idleproc/check errors/user-abort/etc:							lda ParamWordE						;use vertical counter and mask off							and #ImagerILSFrequencyMask			;with all 1's so that we get all-0							bne ImPr_done_intlnstuff			;periodically (ie, every 64 lines)							jsr IntraLineService				;do iproc/monitor/cmd-period activityImPr_done_intlnstuff*If the abort flag is set, for any reason, abort at this time:							lda AbortFlag							bne ImPr_exit							*Increment vertical counters and loop back:							clc									;add the byte-width of the source							lda ParamLongD+0					;bitmap to our current pointer, so							adc SourceByteWidth					;as to point it to the next line							sta ParamLongD+0							lda ParamLongD+2							adc #0							sta ParamLongD+2														inc ParamWordE						;increment vertical counter							lda ParamWordE						;compare against last value							cmp SourceYLineEnd					;loop if not done							bcs ImPr_done_vertical							brl ImPr_vertical_loopImPr_done_vertical*Exclusive exit point; exit with status in ACC/carry:ImPr_exit					lda AbortFlag							cmp #1							rts*Define-graphics-data-rectangle command sequence sent to printer prior to graphics data:ImPrRectCommand				dc.b 10								;length							dc.b $52							;DDR commandImPrRectCommandX1			dc.w 0								;X1/Y1/X2/Y2 coordinates, givenImPrRectCommandY1			dc.w 0								;as words, lo byte firstImPrRectCommandX2			dc.w 0ImPrRectCommandY2			dc.w 0							dc.b $00							;command separator*Draw-empty-scan-line command sequence sent to printer:ImPrBlankLineCommand		dc.b 4								;length							dc.b $47							;transfer-graphics command							dc.w $0001							;graphics length word, lo byte first							dc.b $80							;empty-scanline compression-opcode*Draw-repeat-of-last-scan-line command sequence sent to printer:ImPrRepeatLineCommand		dc.b 4								;length							dc.b $47							;transfer-graphics command							dc.w $0001							;graphics length word, lo byte first							dc.b $C0							;repeat-scanline compression-opcode**COMPRESSSEND: Sends data in the print-pix-buffer to port driver (printer) in compacted format:**This routine analyzes the data in the PrintPixBuffer and then writes into the CompressPixBuffer*a compressed version of the data, according to the compression format.  The total length*of the data sequence is inserted into a raster-transfer command sequence, and then this command*sequence, followed by the compressed data, is output to the port driver with a single write call.**Two subroutines, COMPRESSSENDADDDATANOR and COMPRESSSENDADDDATARLE, are used by this routine.*They add a discrete-data-block or a repeating-data-block to the output CompressPixBuffer; if these*routines are asked to add a block that is greater than the maximum-allowed length, then they*fullfill the request by adding several smaller such blocks.**The two subroutines mentioned above also insure that a byte of value $FF will never occur in the*graphics data stream, as required by the printer to avoid ambiguity with immedate commands.*CompressSend							stz cs_curr_pos						;init logical positions for scan:							stz cs_nor_start					;normal-run start and end, repeat-							stz cs_nor_end						;run start, repeat counter, and							stz cs_rle_start					;state: 0=normal, 1=maybe rle,							stz cs_curr_stat					;2=definetely rle; init for counting							stz cs_rept_ctr						;the length of the entire compressed							stz cs_outbuff_pos					;output ready for sending							lda PrintPixBuffer+0				;init "last group" to be always							ina									;different from first group							sta cs_last_group+0							lda SourceXByteEnd					;setup end position of pr pix buff							sec									;scan as 1/2 the length of scrn pix							sbc SourceXByteBegin				;since scrn pix has 4 pix/byte and							lsr a								;pr pix has 8 pix/byte, and since we							sta cs_end_pos						;double 320 mode so it's the samecs_test						ldy cs_curr_pos						;head of scanning loop							shortm								;cmp current byte against last byte							lda PrintPixBuffer,y							cmp cs_last_group							longm							bne cs_diffcs_same						ldx cs_curr_stat					;curr byte is == to byte last time,							cpx #2								;so dispatch to sameness handlers							bne cs_same_01						;if state=2, going to do fast scancs_same_2					shortm								;set short A/mem for comparisonscs_same_2_floop				iny									;keep incrementing cs_curr_pos in Y							cpy cs_end_pos						;check to see if end of buffer							bcc cs_same_2_fcmp					;if not end proceed to the compare							longm								;else: go to long A, update							sty cs_curr_pos						;cs_curr_pos and exit-end-of-buffer							brl cs_flushcs_same_2_fcmp				cmp PrintPixBuffer,y				;we keep the cmp master value in A							beq cs_same_2_floop					;if still equal, continue w/ A and Y							longm								;else: go to long A, update							sty cs_curr_pos						;cs_curr_pos and exit-diff-case							bra cs_diffcs_same_01					cpx #1								;if state=1, go to its handler							bne cs_same_0						;else, if state=0, go to its handlercs_same_1					inc cs_rept_ctr						;inc rept cnt; if < thresh, continue							lda cs_rept_ctr						;repeat counter can make us go from							cmp #ImagerRLEThreshold-2			;state 1 to state 2 if >= thresh							bcc cs_next							inc cs_curr_stat					;staring run: state=2; do nor output							ldx cs_nor_start					;do normal add-data from nor_start							ldy cs_nor_end						;to nor_end-1 and then continue scan							jsr CompressSendAddDataNor							bra cs_nextcs_same_0					inc cs_curr_stat					;same as last time and in state 0, so							stz cs_rept_ctr						;go to state 1, clr repeat ctr, set							lda cs_curr_pos						;possible repeat-run start position							dea							sta cs_rle_start							bra cs_nextcs_diff						lda cs_curr_stat					;curr byte not == to byte last time,							bne cs_diff_12						;so go to non-equal state handlerscs_diff_0					lda cs_curr_pos						;different and in state 0: state							sta cs_nor_end						;stays 0, and track nor_end with							bra cs_next							;curr_pos and continue scancs_diff_12					cmp #1							bne cs_diff_2cs_diff_1					stz cs_curr_stat					;diff and in state 1: state goes							stz cs_rept_ctr						;to 0, clear repeat counter,							lda cs_curr_pos						;and track nor_end with							sta cs_nor_end						;curr_pos and continue scan							bra cs_nextcs_diff_2					stz cs_curr_stat					;diff and in state 2: state goes							lda cs_curr_pos						;to 0, reset normal start/end,							sta cs_nor_start					;do run-length output							sta cs_nor_end							ldx cs_rle_start					;do rle output from rle_start							ldy cs_curr_pos						;to curr_pos-1, and then							jsr CompressSendAddDataRle			;drop thru to cs_nextcs_next						ldy cs_curr_pos						;next position: set last_group,							shortm								;increment pos, see if done							lda PrintPixBuffer,y				;copy 1 byte from pr pix buffer							sta cs_last_group					;so we can compare to next one							longmcs_next_inc					inc cs_curr_pos						;increment current position,							lda cs_curr_pos						;loop until out of bytes used							cmp cs_end_pos						;in pr pix buff for current							bcs cs_flush						;resolution setting							brl cs_test							;go to top of loop or to end-flushcs_flush					lda cs_curr_stat					;final flush: check state							cmp #2							beq cs_flush2cs_flush01					ldx cs_nor_start					;flush/state=0 or 1: do normal							ldy cs_curr_pos						;output from nor_start to curr_pos-1							jsr CompressSendAddDataNor			;and then go send output command							bra cs_send_cmdcs_flush2					ldx cs_rle_start					;flush/state=2: do rle output from							ldy cs_curr_pos						;rle_start to curr_pos-1							jsr CompressSendAddDataRle			;and drop into send-output-commandcs_send_cmd					lda cs_outbuff_pos					;put length of data in cmd sequence							sta CompressXferCmdLengthWord		;as a word, lo byte firstcs_send_cmd_xmit_grcmd		clc									;assume length still in A							adc #CompressXferCmdEnd-CompressXferCmdBegin							ldx #CompressXferCmdBegin			;xmit bytes for entire cmd and exit							ldy #^CompressXferCmdBegin			;data represents an entire scan line							import CommWriteLong				;length in A, ptr in X and Y							jsr CommWriteLong					;go transmit graph command+datacs_send_cmd_xmit_sepcmd		lda #CompressSeparatorCommand		;also send command separator							import CommWriteShort				;and exit							brl CommWriteShort*Subroutine to add non-repeating graphics data to data in compress-pix-buffer (from->X, to->Y):CompressSendAddDataNor		stx cs_addbuff_from					;save the "from" pos in pr pix buff							dey									;save the "to"-1 pos in pr pix buff							sty cs_addbuff_to							tya									;compute ("to"-1) - "from"							sec							sbc cs_addbuff_from							cmp #$FFFF							;if this result is -1 then exit							bne cs_nor_ok							brl cs_nor_exitcs_nor_ok					ina									;A now has number of bytes to do							sta cs_addbuff_num					;store itcs_nor_check_len			cmp #ImagerRLEMaxPacketLength+1		;cs_addbuff_num in A, check if not							bcc cs_nor_do_add					;too long: if ok, add it and exit														pha									;else save cs_addbuff_num total len							pushword cs_addbuff_to				;and save total "to" value							lda #ImagerRLEMaxPacketLength		;we'll do a chunk of m-1 bytes							sta cs_addbuff_num							dea									;set chunk's "to":=m-1+total"from"-1							clc									;so that we're going from "from"							adc cs_addbuff_from					;to ("from" plus m-1) bytes							sta cs_addbuff_to							jsr cs_nor_do_add					;go do a chunk of m-1 bytes							lda cs_addbuff_to					;set "from" to our "to"+1, so that we							ina									;can continue next chunk where the							sta cs_addbuff_from					;one we just did left off							pullword cs_addbuff_to				;restore original total "to" value							pla									;restore total cs_addbuff_num length							sec									;we've done m-1 bytes of it							sbc #ImagerRLEMaxPacketLength		;so subtract m-1 and store and							sta cs_addbuff_num					;also leave the new value in A							bra cs_nor_check_len				;try again, with cs_addbuff_num in Acs_nor_do_add				shortm								;going to deal with 8-bit bytes							lda cs_addbuff_num+0				;build the %00mmmmmm 0..m opcode							ldy cs_addbuff_from					;get "from" pr pix buff pos in Y							ldx cs_outbuff_pos					;get current out-buff position in X							sta CompressPixBuffer,x				;store the opcode byte in out-buff							inx									;and increment out-buff positioncs_nor_copy_loop			lda PrintPixBuffer,y				;get discrete data byte from pr pix							sta CompressPixBuffer,x				;buff and store into out-buff							inx									;increment our out-buff posn in X							iny									;increment our pr pix buff posn							cpy cs_addbuff_to					;loop for all pr pix bytes to copy							bcc cs_nor_copy_loop				;up to and including the pr pix buff							beq cs_nor_copy_loop				;position given by the "to" value							stx cs_outbuff_pos					;update output-buff position var							longm								;done dealing with 8-bit bytescs_nor_exit					rts*Subroutine to add repeating graphics data to data in compress-pix-buffer (from->X, to->Y):CompressSendAddDataRle		stx cs_addbuff_from					;save the "from" pos in pr pix buff							dey									;save the "to"-1 pos in pr pix buff							sty cs_addbuff_to							tya									;compute ("to"-1) - "from"							sec							sbc cs_addbuff_from							beq cs_rle_exit						;if this result is 0 or -1 then exit							cmp #$FFFF							beq cs_rle_exit							ina									;A now has number of bytes to do							sta cs_addbuff_num					;store itcs_rle_check_len			cmp #ImagerRLEMaxPacketLength+1		;cs_addbuff_num in A, check if not							bcc cs_rle_do_add					;too long: if ok, add it and exit														pha									;else save cs_addbuff_num total len							pushword cs_addbuff_to				;and save total "to" value							lda #ImagerRLEMaxPacketLength		;we'll do a chunk of m-1 bytes							sta cs_addbuff_num							dea									;set chunk's "to":=m-1+total"from"-1							clc									;so that we're going from "from"							adc cs_addbuff_from					;to ("from" plus m-1) bytes							sta cs_addbuff_to							jsr cs_rle_do_add					;go do a chunk of m-1 bytes							lda cs_addbuff_to					;set "from" to our "to"+1, so that we							ina									;can continue next chunk where the							sta cs_addbuff_from					;one we just did left off							pullword cs_addbuff_to				;restore original total "to" value							pla									;restore total cs_addbuff_num length							sec									;we've done m-1 bytes of it							sbc #ImagerRLEMaxPacketLength		;so subtract m-1 and store and							sta cs_addbuff_num					;also leave the new value in A							bra cs_rle_check_len				;try again, with cs_addbuff_num in A							longa off							;set 8-bit-constant code generationcs_rle_do_add				sep #$20							;going to deal with 8-bit bytes							ldx cs_outbuff_pos					;get current out-buff position in X							ldy cs_addbuff_from					;get "from" pr pix buff pos in Y							lda PrintPixBuffer,y				;get the repeatable pr pix data byte							beq cs_rle_do_add_white				;branch if all-white bits in byte							cmp #$FF							;see if all-black bits in byte							bne cs_rle_do_add_mixed				;branch if byte has mixed pixelscs_rle_do_add_black			lda cs_addbuff_num+0				;here if total black byte							;	  76543210							ora #%11000000						;build the %11mmmmmm 0..m opcode							sta CompressPixBuffer,x				;for total black run and output							inx									;increment out-buff position							stx cs_outbuff_pos					;and update out-buff position var							rep #$20							;done with 8-bit bytes and exit							rtscs_rle_do_add_white			lda cs_addbuff_num+0				;here if total white byte							;	  76543210							ora #%10000000						;build the %10mmmmmm 0..m opcode							sta CompressPixBuffer,x				;for total white run and output							inx									;increment out-buff position							stx cs_outbuff_pos					;and update out-buff position var							rep #$20							;done with 8-bit bytes and exit							rtscs_rle_do_add_mixed			pha									;here if mixed data byte, save it							lda cs_addbuff_num+0				;build the %01mmmmmm 0..m opcode							;	  76543210						;for non-black/white repeat run							ora #%01000000							sta CompressPixBuffer,x				;store the opcode byte in out-buff							inx									;and increment out-buff position							pla									;restore data byte in A							sta CompressPixBuffer,x				;and store it into out-buff							inx									;increment our out-buff posn in X							stx cs_outbuff_pos					;update output-buff position var							rep #$20							;done with 8-bit bytes and exitcs_rle_exit					rts							longa on							;back to 16-bit-constants in code*Variables needed by CompressSend and its subroutines:cs_curr_pos					dc.w 0								;current logical position in scancs_end_pos					dc.w 0								;ending posn (#bytes in pr pix buff)cs_curr_stat				dc.w 0								;state: 0=normal; 1=candidate; 2=rlecs_nor_start				dc.w 0								;logical posn of start of normal datacs_nor_end					dc.w 0								;logical posn of end of normal datacs_rle_start				dc.w 0								;logical posn of start of run for rlecs_rept_ctr					dc.w 0								;rept count for run-length candidatecs_last_group				dc.w 0								;value of previous prpix bytecs_outbuff_pos				dc.w 0								;total length of compressed datacs_addbuff_from				dc.w 0								;save "from" param, in add buff subrcs_addbuff_to				dc.w 0								;save "to" param, in add buff subrcs_addbuff_num				dc.w 0								;save "to-from+1", in add buff subrcs_addbuff_num_pvt			dc.w 0								;modifyable copy of cs_addbuff_num**CLEARPRINTPIXBUFFER: Zeroes the printer-ready-pixel line buffer:*ClearPrintPixBuffer			ldx #(PrintPixBufferEnd-PrintPixBuffer)-2							lda #0cl_loop						sta PrintPixBuffer,x				;WARNING: the line buffer length							dex									;must be even for this loop to							dex									;terminate correctly!							bpl cl_loop							rts**INTRALINESERVICE: Idleproc/command-period/abort/error service.  May set abort flag:*IntraLineService***(1) Call IdleProc:							lda IdleProcPtr+0					;call user's idle proc, if any							tax									;if NIL, didn't specify idleproc							ora IdleProcPtr+2					;else build JSL instruction							beq ils_done_iproc														stx ils_goto_iproc+1+0				;iproc may set abort flag so							lda IdleProcPtr+2					;it should be called first before							shortm								;abort flag check below							sta ils_goto_iproc+1+2							longm														phb									;save env, call user, restore							phdils_goto_iproc				jsl $FFFFFF							;NOTE: operand is stuffed							pld							plbils_done_iproc***(2) Peek AbortPoll:							lda AbortPollPtr+0					;check user's abort address							tax									;if NIL, didn't specify abort adrs							ora AbortPollPtr+2					;else build LDA instruction							beq ils_done_abpoll														stx ils_check_abpoll+1+0							lda AbortPollPtr+2							shortm							sta ils_check_abpoll+1+2							longm							ils_check_abpoll			lda >$FFFFFF						;NOTE: operand is stuffed							beq ils_done_abpoll							bra ils_assert_abort				;if user flag nonzero set abortils_done_abpoll***(3) Check Cmd-'.' key:							pha									;check for command-period press							pushword #$0008						;pass keyDownMask							pushlong #ils_eventrec				;pass event record							_GetNextEvent							pla							beq ils_done_abkey							lda ils_event_msg					;check event message for period							and #$00FF							cmp #'.'							bne ils_done_abkey							lda ils_event_mod					;check event modifiers for appleKey							and #$0100							beq ils_done_abkey							bra ils_assert_abort				;if apple-period key, set our abortils_done_abkey***(4) Check communications:							import CommGetAbort					;check if communications still ok							jsr CommGetAbort					;if not ok then fatal error because							cmp #0								;a whole lot of stuff hasn't							beq ils_done_commerror				;gotten through and sync is lost							lda #$8F							;NOTE: a comm error will eventually							bra ils_assert_error_abort_A		;happen on uncorrected printer errils_done_commerror***Normal case exit:							rts									;normal case exit from this routine***Cause abort and exit:ils_assert_abort			lda #$80							;assert the abort flag, which willils_assert_error_abort_A	sta AbortFlag						;will cause an exit out or imager,							rts									;as well as a higher-level abort*Event record used:ils_eventrecils_event_what				dc.w 0ils_event_msg				dc.l 0ils_event_when				dc.l 0ils_event_where				dc.l 0ils_event_mod				dc.w 0**GLOBAL DATA: Variables and data that may be kept across imager calls:*PaperFeed					dc.w 0								;0..1 if auto/man paper feedResolution					dc.w 0								;0/1 if 180/360 dpiVerticalCondenseFlag		dc.w 0								;0 if v 2x (~cond) scaling; 1 if 1xIdleProcPtr					dc.l 0								;ptr to user routine to call or NILAbortPollPtr				dc.l 0								;ptr to adrs to poll for abort or NILSourceMode					dc.w 0								;$00/$80 if 320/640 modeSourcePixPtr				dc.l 0								;pointer to source bitmapSourceByteWidth				dc.w 0								;# of horiz BYTES in a source lineSourceXByteBegin			dc.w 0								;source bitmap X start loop valueSourceXByteEnd				dc.w 0								;source bitmap X end loop valueSourceYLineBegin			dc.w 0								;source bitmap Y start loop valueSourceYLineEnd				dc.w 0								;source bitmap Y end loop valueAbortFlag					dc.w 0								;if nonzero causes our abortPrinterVerticalPosition		dc.w 0								;knowing posn b/w ImagerPrint calls**DATA TABLES: Global lookup tables and buffers needed during the imaging process:*SourceToPrintPixLookup		ds.b 512							;lookup table: source pix -> pr pixPrintPixBuffer				ds.b 360+8							;one raster of pr pix; MUST be even!PrintPixBufferEndCompressXferCmdBegin		CompressXferCmdCommand		dc.b $47							;command sequence and accompanyingCompressXferCmdLengthWord	dc.b 'XX'							;data to print one raster ofCompressXferCmdEnd												;compacted printer pixel data inCompressPixBuffer			ds.b 720+8							;run-length-encoding schemeCompressSeparatorCommand	dc.b 1							dc.b $00							endproc							end